1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
An ML score can improve even when the underlying comparison is not fair. Research Audit Workbench helps researchers and browser agents inspect the evidence before committing more time or compute.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:25,000
This is the real authenticated workflow. I am importing the subtle prepared example: two runs from the same benchmark whose scores appear comparable. The package remains temporary while the application checks it.

3
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Before anything is saved, the preview reconstructs both runs, displays their metrics, inventories every source file, and computes a canonical digest. Confirmation makes this exact evidence package durable and owner-scoped.

4
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The imported pair now becomes an active investigation. The decision question and trusted snapshots are available to both the researcher and the browser agent without copying state into a prompt.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Seven WebMCP tools can inspect the comparison, run the audit, focus evidence, stage a challenge or plan, review readiness, and retrieve a decision brief. Deterministic code owns the findings. Here the candidates, split, and preprocessing match. Both scores even say nDCG at ten, but Run A is micro-averaged while Run B is macro-averaged. The audit preserves both metrics and refuses an unsupported ranking.

6
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The finding cites the exact configuration locations, evidence level, values, and source hashes. Agent prose never becomes the source of truth.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Saving the audit reveals a visible human checkpoint. Because this is a bundled teaching sample, Tab and Enter insert the recommended context. A custom import requires the researcher's own explanation, and only the researcher can confirm it.

8
00:01:48,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The context can revise the intended use of the result, but it cannot erase the metric-definition limitation or its citations. That boundary is retained in the next revision.

9
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Run A is prefilled to Run B's evaluation protocol. Whole-audit validation checks the plan, an operational batch-size change receives a new digest, and the editable rationale binds human approval to that exact version.

10
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The final record is authoritative and durable. WebMCP can inspect and stage work, but it cannot save, approve, delete, or execute.
